# Copy this file to .env and fill in a real value if you want to override the
# backend address for local dev-client/Expo Go use. Never commit .env.
#
# Not needed for ordinary local development — the dev client resolves the
# backend address automatically from Metro's own host (see
# src/shared/config.js). Set this only to force a specific address, e.g. when
# Metro's auto-detected host is wrong for your network setup.
#
# For preview/production EAS builds, this does NOT apply — those read
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL from an EAS environment variable set on the project
# (see SETUP.md), not from this file, because a cloud `eas build` does not
# have access to files that are gitignored on your machine.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.7:5000
